title: $:/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/views/knowledge-mindmap-view
mm.producer: knowledge-tree
mm.args: {"include-areas-root":"yes","collapse-below-depth":"1","node-filter":"[all[shadows+tiddlers]prefix[knowledge/]] +[kn-active-node-filter[]]","node-filter-watch":"[[$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/filter/tiers]] [[$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/filter/types]]"}
mm.preview-top-template: $:/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/templates/preview-top
mm.backlinks-filter: [<previewTitle>ns-backlinks[]]
mm.outgoing-filter: [<previewTitle>ns-forwardlinks[]]

Mindmap view tiddler for the knowledge-app navigation pane.

* `include-areas-root: yes` — forest mode (all areas as roots under a synthetic "Knowledge" root).
* `collapse-below-depth: 1` — area roots stay expanded, their children start collapsed (overlay overrides on user expand and persists across reloads).
* `node-filter` references the `kn-active-node-filter` operator which reads the chip-state tiddlers and narrows the tree to matching `kn.tier` × `kn.type` combinations.
* `node-filter-watch` declares the chip-state tiddlers as reproduce triggers so chip clicks refresh the mindmap.
* `mm.preview-top-template` contributes the `kn.type` pill above the body in the preview pane.
* `mm.backlinks-filter` / `mm.outgoing-filter` use the namespace plugin's `ns-backlinks` / `ns-forwardlinks` (smarter than core `backlinks` / `links` because they follow context-resolution).
